# PeerVault Storage Mesh — see GITIGNORE_AUDIT.md for the audit this file was built from
# (what's ignored and why, what's deliberately still tracked, and any pre-existing gaps found).

# ==============================================================================
# Environment & Secrets
# Real .env files carry real credentials (MONGODB_URI, JWT_SECRET, etc. — see
# backend/.env.example / frontend/.env.example for the documented shape). Template/example
# files are explicitly un-ignored so they stay tracked for anyone cloning the repo.
# ==============================================================================
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Spring Boot local/dev-only profile overrides. Shared profiles that belong in the repo
# (application.yml, application-docker.yml, config-repo/*.yml, etc.) are untouched by this —
# only the personal "-local"/"-dev" override convention is matched.
application-local.yml
application-local.yaml
application-local.properties
application-dev.yml
application-dev.yaml
application-dev.properties

# Local secret/credential/key material. Nothing under these names should ever be real and
# committed — if a template is ever needed, name it *.example.* instead, which these patterns
# don't touch.
secrets/
credentials/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
*.crt
*.cer

# ==============================================================================
# Java / Maven
# ==============================================================================
target/
*.class
*.jar
*.war
# If a Maven wrapper is ever added, its checked-in jar must stay tracked despite the *.jar rule
# above — this repo has no wrapper today, but the negation is cheap insurance against that
# common footgun.
!.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar

# ==============================================================================
# Node / Frontend
# ==============================================================================
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.next/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ==============================================================================
# Build Artifacts (generic)
# ==============================================================================
out/
coverage/

# ==============================================================================
# Logs & Runtime
# ==============================================================================
*.log
logs/
*.pid
*.tmp

# ==============================================================================
# IDE / Editor
# JetBrains project state is always personal (this repo has Java modules, so IntelliJ is a
# realistic choice). VS Code's *team-shared* config is intentionally kept tracked — only the
# rest of .vscode/ (personal window/workspace state) is ignored.
# ==============================================================================
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json

# Claude Code local session/runtime state — mirrors this machine's own (untracked)
# .git/info/exclude, promoted here so it's enforced on every clone, not just this one.
# .claude/settings.json, agents/, and skills/ are shared team config and are NOT matched.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
.claude/routines/.state/
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/checkpoints/
.claude/mailbox/
.claude/agent-registry.json
.claude/agent-memory-local/
.claude/first-run
.claude/assistant-daemon-state.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# ==============================================================================
# OS Files
# ==============================================================================
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ==============================================================================
# Testing / Coverage
# (Maven's surefire/failsafe reports land under each module's target/, already covered above.)
# ==============================================================================
test-results/
reports/

# ==============================================================================
# Docker / Local Development
# The tracked backend/docker-compose.yml stays as-is — only a personal override layered on
# top of it is ignored.
# ==============================================================================
docker-compose.override.yml

# ==============================================================================
# Temporary Files
# ==============================================================================
.cache/
.tmp/
